\id 2JN - Open English Translation—Readers’ Version (OET-RV) v0.2.1
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h 2 John
\toc1 The second letter that we have, written by John
\toc2 2 John
\mt2 The second letter
\mt2 that we have, written by
\mt1 John
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\c 1
\p
\v 1 \add This letter is from John\add* the elder to the chosen lady and her children who I genuinely love (as do all the other believers)
\v 2 because of the truth that lives in us and will be with us forever.
\p
\v 3 We will have grace, mercy, and peace in truth and love from God the father and from his son Jesus \add the\add* messiah.
\s1 Stick to the original message
\p
\v 4 I was so happy that I found some of your children living out the truth as per the command that the father gave us.
\v 5 So now I’m requesting you, lady, (not making some new command, but one that we’ve had since the beginning) that we all need to love each other
\v 6 where the definition of love is obeying God’s commands. This is the command about walking in love that you all heard from the beginning
\v 7 because many false preachers have entered the world who don’t believe that Jesus is \add the\add* messiah who came as a human. Any person like that is a deceiver and against the messiah.
\p
\v 8 So make sure that you all don’t lose what you’ve worked for, but rather go on to receive a full reward.
\p
\v 9 Anyone who doesn’t stay with the messiah’s teaching or adds more to it doesn’t have God—it’s the person who continues in the teaching that has both the father and the son with them.
\v 10 If anyone comes to you all and doesn’t bring this same message, don’t accept that person into your house, and don’t tell them that it’s good
\v 11 because anyone who encourages those people is participating in the evil that they’re spreading.
\s1 Closing off
\p
\v 12 I’ve got many things that I wanted to write to you about, but paper and ink aren’t working for me so I’ll try to come and then we can talk directly because I want you all to experience genuine happiness.
\p
\v 13 Your sister’s children (and she’s \add also\add* a chosen one) send their greetings \add also\add*.
